1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,506
Every service department runs on handovers.

2
00:00:02,806 --> 00:00:05,770
A technician scribbles a note, then the shift ends.

3
00:00:06,070 --> 00:00:09,967
A manager chases answers across notes, calls and screens.

4
00:00:10,267 --> 00:00:14,721
Time goes into asking, searching and re-typing, not fixing cars.

5
00:00:15,021 --> 00:00:17,433
And the real risk hides between shifts.

6
00:00:18,233 --> 00:00:22,682
A safety finding sits in a technician's note that nobody has time to read.

7
00:00:22,982 --> 00:00:26,879
Right now, 12 vehicles on this floor are unsafe to release.

8
00:00:27,779 --> 00:00:30,374
That's where the Service Operations Agent comes in.

9
00:00:31,174 --> 00:00:35,068
Here is how it works. A technician speaks or types an update.

10
00:00:35,368 --> 00:00:39,587
NVIDIA Riva transcribes it, and Nemotron extracts the facts.

11
00:00:39,887 --> 00:00:42,853
Code checks every fact. Nothing is guessed.

12
00:00:43,153 --> 00:00:45,193
Each update joins an audit trail.

13
00:00:45,493 --> 00:00:50,503
So a manager simply asks, and gets a cited answer. Now, the real thing.

14
00:00:51,603 --> 00:00:55,079
Watch. A technician dictates an update from the bay.

15
00:00:55,379 --> 00:00:58,018
NVIDIA Riva turns the speech into text.

16
00:00:58,318 --> 00:01:02,121
Nemotron pulls out the facts: the measurement, and the spec.

17
00:01:03,221 --> 00:01:07,678
Code checks it, and flags the repair order unsafe to release, instantly.

18
00:01:09,278 --> 00:01:11,877
Now the manager asks the question that matters.

19
00:01:12,177 --> 00:01:15,052
Which vehicles cannot be released on safety grounds?

20
00:01:15,352 --> 00:01:22,216
13 vehicles. Every one cited. Answered in a tenth of a second, with no model call.

21
00:01:23,016 --> 00:01:27,698
Now an open question: has anyone seen a whistling noise on a Passat?

22
00:01:27,998 --> 00:01:32,730
Search, rerank and a cited answer, in seconds, on the same GPU.

23
00:01:33,830 --> 00:01:36,099
Unsafe vehicles surface at once.

24
00:01:36,399 --> 00:01:38,854
Managers get answers in a tenth of a second.

25
00:01:39,154 --> 00:01:41,613
Every figure traces back to a real record.

26
00:01:41,913 --> 00:01:45,485
And one update feeds the record, handover and dashboard.

27
00:01:46,085 --> 00:01:51,469
The deployed architecture: three NVIDIA NIMs on one L40S.

28
00:01:52,169 --> 00:01:56,624
Riva handles speech. NeMo Guardrails stops unsafe requests.

29
00:01:56,924 --> 00:02:00,914
NeMo Evaluator scores every release. That is the whole stack.

30
00:02:02,414 --> 00:02:08,068
Observability is built in: DCGM and the app's own metrics, live in Grafana.

31
00:02:08,868 --> 00:02:15,735
In short, in numbers: 12 of 32 unsafe vehicles flagged the moment an update is logged.

32
00:02:16,035 --> 00:02:20,955
Answers in a tenth of a second, every figure traced, all on one L40S.

33
00:02:21,255 --> 00:02:26,546
Fast. Grounded. Yours to run. That is the Service Operations Agent.

